\section{Related Work}
Several prominent approaches for using AI in satellite image analysis have gained significant traction. Transferring models from image datasets to satellite images and using meta-learning are also major areas of focus. Despite these efforts, leveraging AI in satellite images for real-world applications remains challenging due to issues with scale, diversity, and complexity. To address this problem, we have developed a flexible and adaptable architecture for multi-modal datasets that incorporates meta-learning and data augmentation. 

